WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:05.556
You read a fictional tenant's P R V
groups against a reviewed file of four,

3
00:00:05.556 --> 00:00:10.475
and found a standing member nobody granted,
an owner trap, and a nested group.

4
00:00:10.475 --> 00:00:13.577
You read the exact requests
that would fix them,

5
00:00:13.577 --> 00:00:18.666
saw a guard refuse a plan with too many
removals, saw the apply refuse to select

6
00:00:18.666 --> 00:00:23.438
c1 until a person confirmed the gate,
and applied ten requests to the fake.

7
00:00:23.438 --> 00:00:27.226
Next is Module 6: PIM for Azure resources.

8
00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:30.382
Owner, Contributor and
User Access Administrator

9
00:00:30.382 --> 00:00:32.712
on a subscription are privileged too.

10
00:00:32.712 --> 00:00:36.752
PIM for Azure resources isn't in
Microsoft Graph: it goes through

11
00:00:36.752 --> 00:00:41.249
Azure Resource Manager, with Azure
roles instead of Graph permissions.

12
00:00:41.249 --> 00:00:45.473
In Module 6 you hold it as
code, with the same discipline:

13
00:00:45.473 --> 00:00:48.170
read, diff, and send only with Apply.
